Package: NAAAntoka
Title: Tools for NAAA Data Preparation
Version: 0.0.1.9008
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Lanlanbow",
           email = "66890428+Lanlanbow@users.noreply.github.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tools to prepare National Assessment of Academic Ability (NAAA)
    data. Exports metadata filtered by survey category, years, and keywords
    with familiar selection helpers and regular expressions to editable
    text-preserving Excel mapping files, grouping matches by search term and
    survey year for review. Reads those files
    directly to name selected columns and locate yearly survey CSV files.
    Converts UTF-8 and CP932 CSV files into UTF-8 copies with streaming
    operating-system tools, preserving source files and existing output when
    conversion fails. Searches variable names and labels from a metadata
    folder explicitly selected for the R session by keyword
    while preserving source metadata and unverified definitions. Creates
    analyst-defined concepts from selected variables and records their years,
    rationale, and catalog version. Supports long-format metadata with
    code-label dictionaries and compares choices, including nonresponse
    codes, without recoding responses. Reads selected
    UTF-8 CSV columns, combines concept and original-variable selections in
    the same read, filters Gregorian or Japanese era survey years, and
    stacks records across years with explicit exclusion reports. The package
    is being rebuilt one feature at a time.
